{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310827,"nonce":"o9aYsJoLw6TYzJ/wAn3Msowp+UU=","title":"The published conformance score is a CRANELIFT score. LLVM=1 scores 372 vs the default path's 364, and the two tiers disagree on 83 tests. ...","message":"**The default corpus run never exercises LLVM at all.** Every preset sets\n`auto_upgrade_to_llvm_after_main_entry: false`, and the corpus runs\n`--preset application`, so `upgrade_to_llvm()` is called ZERO times across all\n1030 tests. The score is Cranelift plus whatever Beadie/OSR promotes on code a\nshort test makes hot -- nearly nothing. Zero `LLVM upgrade failed` lines in a\ncorpus log means the tier was never asked, NOT that it is healthy.\n\nScore the other tier with (added ec9a4dce):\n\n    LLVM=1 ./haxe-conformance/run.sh\n\n\n| outcome | default | LLVM |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| PASS | 364 | **372** |\n| CRASH | 225 | 173 |\n| COMPILE_FAIL | 259 | 287 |\n| WRONG_ANSWER | 179 | 191 |\n\n**83 tests differ between tiers.** 19 pass only under LLVM; **11 pass only under\nthe default path, 3 of them CRASHING under LLVM** -- those are real LLVM-tier\ndefects and the most valuable rows in the whole corpus.\n\nLargest movements: `CRASH -\u003e WRONG_ANSWER` x22 and `CRASH -\u003e COMPILE_FAIL` x19.\nLLVM compiles the whole module up front, so it REJECTS at compile time what the\ntiered path only discovers by crashing at run time.\n\n\n- `run.sh` runs under `set -u` and macOS ships **bash 3.2**, where `\"${arr[@]}\"`\n  on an EMPTY array is an unbound-variable error. An optional-flag array there\n  fails every invocation and scores the whole corpus COMPILE_FAIL. It looks like\n  a catastrophic tier difference; it is a harness bug. A result wildly off a\n  known baseline is a broken measurement, not a finding.\n- `rayzor run --llvm` tree-shakes before compiling, so an UNCALLED broken\n  function is never lowered or verified. `scripts/check_llvm_tier.sh` compiles\n  every body and is the real tier gate.\n- An explicit `--llvm` whose upgrade fails is now FATAL (dab0d880); it used to\n  warn and continue on Cranelift, making every number from that run a Cranelift\n  number under another name.\n\n\n    CRANELIFT=1 ./haxe-conformance/run.sh     # --tier 1, start compiled, no promotion\n\nThe default run is NOT a Cranelift run -- it starts interpreted and climbs, so a\ntest too short to get hot is scored largely on the INTERPRETER. Pinning matters.\n\nThree configurations, one commit, one machine, 1165 tests:\n\n| config | PASS |\n|---|---:|\n| default | 364 |\n| cranelift (pinned) | 364 |\n| llvm | 372 |\n\n**default and cranelift PASS the SAME SET** -- identical, with one status\ndifference in 1165. The published score is a Cranelift score exactly.\n\n\nTwo tiers agreeing against a third is evidence, not a guess. It finds defects\nBOTH ways:\n\n**11 LLVM-tier defects** (pass on default AND cranelift, fail on llvm):\n- WRONG_ANSWER, silent, most serious: Issue4649, Issue5289, Issue8849\n- CRASH: Issue2713, Issue2874, Issue4460\n- COMPILE_FAIL: Issue3212, Issue4617, Issue6067, Issue6430, Issue7220\n\n**19 Cranelift-tier defects** (pass under llvm ONLY): Issue2627, Issue2835,\nIssue3447, Issue3792, Issue3852, Issue4000, Issue4001, Issue4360, Issue4798,\nIssue4986, Issue5124, Issue5558, and 7 more -- see a fresh run.\n\nSame rule as [[bugs-simd-round-disagreed-across-tiers]]: a construct's semantics\nare the INTERSECTION of the backends, and any single-tier disagreement is a bug\nin that tier.\n\n- Index summary moved from MEMORY.md (2026-10-18): The published score is a CRANELIFT score: default never calls upgrade_to_llvm once. `LLVM=1 ./run.sh` = 372 vs 364, and 83 tests DISAGREE between tiers (11 pass only on default, 3 crash under LLVM).\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_conformance_tiers_disagree_llvm_vs_default` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}